WEBVTT

00:00:01.123 --> 00:00:32.474
Smallville Arrival Based on a novelization by Michael Teitelbaum Arrival Chapter 1 A Child Arrives 1989, Smallville, Kansas, USA.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.978
Suddenly, the sky was dark.

00:00:36.038 --> 00:00:39.180
There were hundreds of meteors in the sky.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.493
They went faster and faster.

00:00:42.553 --> 00:00:47.557
There was a very small spaceship in the center of the meteors.

00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:53.510
There was one person in this spaceship, a child.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.840
Nothing happened in Smallville.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:02.534
It was a small town in Kansas, and it was a very boring place.

00:01:02.594 --> 00:01:07.288
Then one day, everything changed.

00:01:07.348 --> 00:01:12.672
Lionel Luther arrived from Metropolis in his helicopter.

00:01:12.732 --> 00:01:17.086
He was a rich man, but he was not a nice man.

00:01:17.146 --> 00:01:20.319
He loved money, not people.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:23.928
His young son Lex sat next to him.

00:01:23.988 --> 00:01:26.614
Lex was nine years old.

00:01:26.674 --> 00:01:29.838
He had red hair and blue eyes.

00:01:29.898 --> 00:01:33.922
His face was white, and his eyes were closed.

00:01:33.982 --> 00:01:36.384
He was very frightened.

00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:41.968
Lex shouted his father, open your eyes now.

00:01:42.028 --> 00:01:44.810
I can't, Lex said.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.432
I hate this helicopter.

00:01:47.492 --> 00:01:52.148
Luther's aren't frightened of anything, Lionel said.

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:55.982
Look out of the window, now!"

00:01:56.042 --> 00:02:00.357
Lex slowly opened his eyes and looked down.

00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:04.281
I'm going to die, he thought.

00:02:04.341 --> 00:02:09.426
Two men waited for the helicopter in the car park of an old factory.

00:02:09.486 --> 00:02:14.301
The men were brothers, Dale and Bill Ross.

00:02:14.361 --> 00:02:18.794
Why does Lionel Luther want to buy our factory?"

00:02:18.854 --> 00:02:20.526
asked Dale.

00:02:20.586 --> 00:02:23.338
I don't know, said Bill.

00:02:23.397 --> 00:02:25.760
But we need his money.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:28.231
He isn't going to change anything.

00:02:28.291 --> 00:02:32.314
He told us that, and I believe him.

00:02:32.374 --> 00:02:38.950
Jonathan Kent and his wife Martha went into a shop on Main Street.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.666
Their faces were brown from the sun, and their jeans were old.

00:02:43.726 --> 00:02:46.076
They lived on a farm.

00:02:46.136 --> 00:02:48.078
Afternoon, Nell.

00:02:48.138 --> 00:02:49.759
Jonathan said.

00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:51.560
Hello, Jonathan.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.651
Nell said.

00:02:52.711 --> 00:02:54.202
She smiled at him.

00:02:54.262 --> 00:02:56.173
She liked Jonathan.

00:02:56.233 --> 00:02:58.094
Hello, Martha.

00:02:58.154 --> 00:02:59.385
She said.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.736
She didn't smile at Martha.

00:03:01.796 --> 00:03:03.695
She didn't like her.

00:03:03.755 --> 00:03:08.064
I'd like some tulips, said Martha.

00:03:08.124 --> 00:03:11.055
A red tulips, please.

00:03:11.115 --> 00:03:14.036
There was a little girl in the shop.

00:03:14.096 --> 00:03:16.777
She was very pretty with dark hair.

00:03:16.837 --> 00:03:19.278
She was three years old.

00:03:19.337 --> 00:03:22.999
Hello, Lana, said Martha.

00:03:23.059 --> 00:03:25.970
Where are your mum and dad today?

00:03:26.029 --> 00:03:29.981
They're at the homecoming game, Nell said.

00:03:30.041 --> 00:03:32.002
Here are your tulips.

00:03:32.062 --> 00:03:34.747
She gave them to Jonathan.

00:03:34.807 --> 00:03:38.594
In the street, Martha said sadly.

00:03:38.654 --> 00:03:43.478
Oh, Jonathan, I looked at Lana's little face, didn't I?

00:03:43.538 --> 00:03:45.170
She stopped.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.422
I know, Martha, said Jonathan.

00:03:48.482 --> 00:03:51.344
We both want a child.

00:03:51.404 --> 00:03:55.758
The meteors came closer and closer.

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:59.481
At the factory, Lex was bored.

00:03:59.541 --> 00:04:03.956
He walked away into a cornfield next to the factory.

00:04:04.016 --> 00:04:07.109
Lionel Luther read the papers.

00:04:07.169 --> 00:04:09.500
Where do I put my name?

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.781
He asked the Ross brothers.

00:04:11.841 --> 00:04:13.422
He smiled.

00:04:13.482 --> 00:04:16.132
The factory was his now.

00:04:16.192 --> 00:04:20.955
Alone in the field, Lex suddenly heard something.

00:04:21.014 --> 00:04:22.976
Help me!

00:04:23.036 --> 00:04:24.706
What was it?

00:04:24.766 --> 00:04:26.627
Then he heard it again.

00:04:26.687 --> 00:04:29.398
Help me!

00:04:29.458 --> 00:04:35.264
He walked through the corn, and suddenly there was a scarecrow.

00:04:35.324 --> 00:04:37.620
Lex was frightened.

00:04:37.679 --> 00:04:41.432
That scarecrow can talk, he thought.

00:04:41.492 --> 00:04:44.055
But then it wasn't a scarecrow.

00:04:44.115 --> 00:04:46.427
It was a teenage boy.

00:04:46.487 --> 00:04:49.640
The boy was on a big wooden pole.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.742
He had no shirt.

00:04:51.802 --> 00:04:56.056
There was a big red S on the front of his body.

00:04:56.116 --> 00:04:58.538
Help me, please!

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:01.766
He said one more time.

00:05:01.826 --> 00:05:07.215
The first big meteor crashed into the cornfield.

00:05:07.275 --> 00:05:08.446
Lex ran.

00:05:08.466 --> 00:05:14.480
A car stopped opposite Nell's shop on Main Street.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:19.364
Nell took little Lana in her arms and walked out of the shop.

00:05:19.424 --> 00:05:22.466
Lewis and Laura Lang were in the car.

00:05:22.526 --> 00:05:24.178
Lana saw them.

00:05:24.238 --> 00:05:25.238
Mommy!

00:05:25.298 --> 00:05:26.199
Daddy!

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:27.700
She shouted.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:34.003
Nell looked up and saw a big meteor in the sky.

00:05:34.063 --> 00:05:38.972
The meteor crashed into the Lang's car.

00:05:39.032 --> 00:05:42.886
Lana's parents were dead.

00:05:42.946 --> 00:05:46.611
Lionel Luther ran across the cornfield.

00:05:46.671 --> 00:05:48.882
Lex, where are you?

00:05:48.942 --> 00:05:50.252
He shouted.

00:05:50.312 --> 00:05:53.184
He saw some red hair on the ground.

00:05:53.244 --> 00:05:55.845
Then he found his son.

00:05:55.905 --> 00:05:58.076
Lex was on the ground.

00:05:58.136 --> 00:06:00.137
He was very frightened.

00:06:00.197 --> 00:06:03.138
But where was his beautiful red hair?

00:06:03.198 --> 00:06:08.951
He was nine years old, and he now had no hair at all.

00:06:09.011 --> 00:06:13.454
Jonathan and Martha Kent were on their way home.

00:06:13.514 --> 00:06:17.268
Suddenly, a meteor hit the road behind them.

00:06:17.328 --> 00:06:19.489
What was that, Jonathan?

00:06:19.549 --> 00:06:21.070
asked Martha.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.902
What's happening?

00:06:22.962 --> 00:06:24.692
Boom!

00:06:24.752 --> 00:06:28.466
A spaceship crashed into the road in front of them.

00:06:28.525 --> 00:06:33.673
Jonathan tried to stop the car, but it crashed into a cornfield.

00:06:33.733 --> 00:06:37.698
When they opened their eyes, they saw a boy.

00:06:37.758 --> 00:06:42.559
He was about three years old and he had no clothes.

00:06:42.619 --> 00:06:45.800
The boy pulled Jonathan's car door.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.190
It opened.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.901
Then he pulled Martha's car door.

00:06:49.961 --> 00:06:51.671
It opened too.

00:06:51.731 --> 00:06:55.502
Martha and Jonathan were very surprised.

00:06:55.562 --> 00:06:58.042
They were soon out of the car.

00:06:58.102 --> 00:07:02.428
Martha took the boy in her arms.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:06.475
Yes, I'm fine.

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:07.426
You?

00:07:07.486 --> 00:07:09.077
said Martha.

00:07:09.137 --> 00:07:14.952
But yes, children don't fall from the sky, Jonathan said.

00:07:15.012 --> 00:07:17.875
Then where did he come from?

00:07:17.935 --> 00:07:19.556
Martha asked.

00:07:19.616 --> 00:07:23.160
I don't think his mum and dad are from Kansas.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:26.723
We can't keep him, Martha, said Jonathan.

00:07:26.783 --> 00:07:28.934
What can we say to people?

00:07:28.994 --> 00:07:31.900
We found him in a cornfield?

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:36.786
We didn't find him Jonathan, said Martha.

00:07:36.846 --> 00:07:45.538
He found us.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:08:01.424
Chapter 2 Special and Different Jonathan and Martha took the boy home to their farm.

00:08:01.484 --> 00:08:03.696
They named him Clark.

00:08:03.756 --> 00:08:06.879
They didn't tell him about his arrival.

00:08:06.939 --> 00:08:09.492
They didn't tell other people either.

00:08:09.552 --> 00:08:14.766
If someone asked, they said, he's Martha's sister's son.

00:08:14.826 --> 00:08:16.496
She died.

00:08:16.556 --> 00:08:22.396
They didn't want Clark to be different from other children, but he was different.

00:08:22.456 --> 00:08:24.046
He was special.

00:08:24.106 --> 00:08:26.087
He was very strong.

00:08:26.147 --> 00:08:28.118
He was very fast.

00:08:28.178 --> 00:08:30.379
Nothing hurt him.

00:08:30.438 --> 00:08:34.920
When he was eight, a big milk can hit his head.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:39.212
It didn't hurt him.

00:08:39.272 --> 00:08:43.493
2001 Smallville, Kansas, USA.

00:08:43.553 --> 00:08:46.430
Clark sat at his computer.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:49.248
Every morning he used the internet.

00:08:49.308 --> 00:08:55.721
He wanted to find stories about special people, very strong people, very fast people.

00:08:55.741 --> 00:08:58.182
"'Clark, Kent!'

00:08:58.242 --> 00:08:59.163
Martha called.

00:08:59.183 --> 00:09:01.605
"'You're going to be late for the bus.'

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:04.536
"'Okay, I'm coming!'

00:09:04.596 --> 00:09:06.248
shouted Clark.

00:09:06.308 --> 00:09:14.836
He put on his school clothes and shoes, cleaned his room and put his school books in his bag, all in one minute.

00:09:14.896 --> 00:09:18.472
Martha came into his room with some clothes.

00:09:18.532 --> 00:09:23.466
You can wear these to the homecoming dance this weekend, she said.

00:09:23.526 --> 00:09:26.748
I'm not going, Mum, said Clark.

00:09:26.808 --> 00:09:29.310
I haven't got a girl to go with.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.261
Did you ask anyone?

00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:32.792
Martha asked.

00:09:32.853 --> 00:09:34.854
No, he said.

00:09:34.914 --> 00:09:37.200
He ran down to the kitchen.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.497
What's that letter, son?"

00:09:39.557 --> 00:09:41.258
asked Jonathan.

00:09:41.318 --> 00:09:44.529
It's for the football team, said Clark.

00:09:44.589 --> 00:09:46.980
They want some new players.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:50.362
You can't do it, said Jonathan.

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:53.554
Oh, please, Dad, said Clark.

00:09:53.614 --> 00:09:55.434
I can run slowly.

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:57.426
I can be careful.

00:09:57.486 --> 00:10:02.808
I'm sorry, Clark, said Jonathan, but the answer is no.

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:06.628
I don't want to be different, shouted Clark.

00:10:06.688 --> 00:10:09.128
I can never do normal things.

00:10:09.188 --> 00:10:11.789
People at school think I'm a loser."

00:10:11.849 --> 00:10:14.120
He ran out of the door.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.242
We must tell him about the spaceship.

00:10:17.302 --> 00:10:19.800
Martha said to Jonathan.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.638
Clark walked to the bus stop.

00:10:22.698 --> 00:10:24.229
He was late again.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:27.032
The school bus drove off without him.

00:10:27.092 --> 00:10:28.583
Oh no!

00:10:28.643 --> 00:10:32.016
He said, everything's going wrong today.

00:10:32.076 --> 00:10:35.799
Suddenly, he smiled a big smile.

00:10:35.859 --> 00:10:41.694
He turned and ran through the field at a hundred kilometers an hour.

00:10:41.754 --> 00:10:44.596
The bus arrived at school.

00:10:44.656 --> 00:10:48.976
Clark's friends Pete Ross and Chloe Sullivan were on it.

00:10:49.036 --> 00:10:51.672
Chloe was new in Smallville.

00:10:51.732 --> 00:10:54.364
Her dad worked at Luther Corps.

00:10:54.424 --> 00:10:58.646
She wrote for the school newspaper and took photos for it.

00:10:58.706 --> 00:11:02.138
She was always ready with her camera.

00:11:02.198 --> 00:11:05.229
Are you going to the dance with anyone?

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.010
Pete asked Chloe.

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:10.452
No, not yet, said Chloe.

00:11:10.512 --> 00:11:14.114
Well, if Clark doesn't ask you.

00:11:14.174 --> 00:11:18.076
I'm not interested in Clark, Pete, she said.

00:11:18.137 --> 00:11:19.392
Right.

00:11:19.452 --> 00:11:20.806
said Pete.

00:11:20.866 --> 00:11:23.008
He knew that wasn't true.

00:11:23.068 --> 00:11:28.062
Well, we can go to the dance together if you want, he said.

00:11:28.122 --> 00:11:32.064
Not boy and girl, friend and friend.

00:11:32.124 --> 00:11:34.636
Suddenly Clark was there.

00:11:34.696 --> 00:11:37.408
Hi you too, he said.

00:11:37.468 --> 00:11:41.480
Pete and Chloe were very surprised to see their friend.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:44.692
We saw you at your farm, Chloe said.

00:11:44.752 --> 00:11:46.823
You weren't on the bus.

00:11:46.883 --> 00:11:50.488
I came a different way, said Clark.

00:11:50.548 --> 00:11:53.282
Are you ready for the football team, Clark?

00:11:53.342 --> 00:11:54.774
asked Pete.

00:11:54.834 --> 00:11:58.219
I'm not going to do it, said Clark.

00:11:58.279 --> 00:12:00.843
But Clark said Pete.

00:12:00.903 --> 00:12:03.368
Do you want to be the scarecrow?

00:12:03.428 --> 00:12:06.780
The scarecrow, Chloe said loudly.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:08.780
What's the scarecrow?

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:11.141
Shh, said Pete.

00:12:11.201 --> 00:12:15.642
This happens here every year Chloe, before the homecoming game.

00:12:15.702 --> 00:12:20.053
The football players choose someone, a loser.

00:12:20.113 --> 00:12:24.334
They take him to the cornfield and take all his clothes.

00:12:24.394 --> 00:12:28.168
Then they write a big red S on the front of his body.

00:12:28.228 --> 00:12:32.074
And they put him on a big wooden pole, said Clark.

00:12:32.134 --> 00:12:34.686
So he's a scarecrow.

00:12:34.746 --> 00:12:37.998
How terrible, said Chloe.

00:12:38.058 --> 00:12:44.492
Then Clark saw a beautiful girl with long brown hair and a lovely smile.

00:12:44.552 --> 00:12:48.396
See you later, he said to his friends.

00:12:48.456 --> 00:12:51.908
Clark walked across to Lana Lang.

00:12:51.968 --> 00:12:53.909
He was a meter from her.

00:12:53.969 --> 00:12:56.401
Suddenly he crashed to the ground.

00:12:56.461 --> 00:12:58.684
His books went everywhere.

00:12:58.744 --> 00:13:02.820
Why does this always happen, near Lana, you thought?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.150
Is it because I like her?

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:06.772
Hi, Clark.

00:13:06.832 --> 00:13:08.093
Are you okay?

00:13:08.153 --> 00:13:09.444
She asked.

00:13:09.504 --> 00:13:10.695
Hi, Lana.

00:13:10.754 --> 00:13:13.776
He said, yeah, I'm fine.

00:13:13.836 --> 00:13:16.008
She gave his books to him.

00:13:16.068 --> 00:13:18.310
You're reading Nietzsche, huh?

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:20.962
Are you man or Superman?

00:13:21.022 --> 00:13:24.034
I don't know, Clark said.

00:13:24.094 --> 00:13:25.910
They smiled.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:31.729
Lana shouted Whitney Fordman, a tall, good-looking student.

00:13:31.789 --> 00:13:34.010
He was Lana's boyfriend.

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.803
Whitney was fantastic at sports.

00:13:36.863 --> 00:13:39.224
He was in all the school teams.

00:13:39.284 --> 00:13:41.916
He ran up and kissed Lana.

00:13:41.976 --> 00:13:50.520
They walked away together.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:58.594
Chapter 3.

00:13:58.654 --> 00:14:05.730
Two terrible shocks A student looked at the photos of the school sports teams.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:09.304
He looked at the 1989 photo.

00:14:09.364 --> 00:14:12.337
Your lake for your class, young man?

00:14:12.397 --> 00:14:14.349
Said a teacher behind him.

00:14:14.409 --> 00:14:16.170
The student turned.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.702
What's your name?

00:14:17.762 --> 00:14:19.244
Asked the teacher.

00:14:19.304 --> 00:14:20.842
Are you new?

00:14:20.902 --> 00:14:24.941
Suddenly, the student hit the teacher in the face.

00:14:25.001 --> 00:14:30.883
A big blue electric shock went from the student's hand into the teacher's body.

00:14:30.943 --> 00:14:33.814
The teacher crashed into the wall.

00:14:33.874 --> 00:14:39.756
The student took the photo of the three happy football players and left the school.

00:14:39.816 --> 00:14:43.737
I'm gonna get you, he thought.

00:14:43.797 --> 00:14:50.580
Lex Luther drove his Porsche through the country to the Luther Court factory in Smallville.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:54.594
The Smallville factory doesn't make any money.

00:14:54.654 --> 00:15:00.038
Lionel Luther said to his son, go to Smallville, make changes.

00:15:00.098 --> 00:15:07.802
So Lex left Metropolis, and here he was, in the center of nowhere, great.

00:15:07.862 --> 00:15:10.664
Lex arrived at Luther Corps.

00:15:10.724 --> 00:15:15.506
He was 21 years old, and he still had no hair.

00:15:15.566 --> 00:15:18.278
He walked into the factory.

00:15:18.338 --> 00:15:21.660
A man sat at a desk with his lunch.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:25.472
Mr. Luther, the man said surprised.

00:15:25.532 --> 00:15:27.914
My name's Gabe Sullivan.

00:15:27.974 --> 00:15:29.886
Call me Lex.

00:15:29.945 --> 00:15:33.778
The workers aren't happy, Lex, said Gabe.

00:15:33.838 --> 00:15:36.420
They're frightened about their jobs.

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.991
It's okay, said Lex.

00:15:39.051 --> 00:15:41.563
I want everyone to stay.

00:15:41.623 --> 00:15:48.890
But your father said, I'm not my father, said Lex Luther.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:55.198
Later, Lex drove down a small country road at a hundred kilometers an hour.

00:15:55.257 --> 00:15:58.380
His car radio played loud music.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:02.264
Not far away, Clark was on a bridge.

00:16:02.324 --> 00:16:04.387
He looked into the water.

00:16:04.446 --> 00:16:08.170
He thought about his life, and he wasn't happy.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.643
He didn't hear Lex Luther's car.

00:16:11.703 --> 00:16:14.766
Lex answered his mobile phone.

00:16:14.826 --> 00:16:17.058
He didn't look at the road for a minute.

00:16:17.118 --> 00:16:19.200
He drove onto the bridge.

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:21.592
Then he saw Clark.

00:16:21.652 --> 00:16:26.206
He tried to stop the car, but Clark was right in front of him.

00:16:26.266 --> 00:16:29.248
I'm going to hit him, Lex thought.

00:16:29.308 --> 00:16:31.050
Their eyes met.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:34.352
Then Lex's car crashed into Clark.

00:16:34.412 --> 00:16:36.034
Boom!

00:16:36.094 --> 00:16:40.858
The car and Clark went over the bridge and into the water.

00:16:40.918 --> 00:16:51.684
Clark's eyes closed and everything went black.

00:16:51.744 --> 00:17:06.713
Chapter 4 The Green Necklace Under the water, Clark opened his eyes.

00:17:06.773 --> 00:17:08.413
He was okay.

00:17:08.473 --> 00:17:10.294
He wasn't hurt.

00:17:10.354 --> 00:17:12.734
Then he remembered the car.

00:17:12.794 --> 00:17:14.335
The car!

00:17:14.395 --> 00:17:17.346
He found the car with Lex in it.

00:17:17.406 --> 00:17:19.676
Lex's eyes were closed.

00:17:19.736 --> 00:17:23.318
Clark pulled open the door and pulled Lex out.

00:17:23.378 --> 00:17:27.129
He took him in his arms and started to swim.

00:17:27.189 --> 00:17:31.885
When Clark put Lex on the ground, he thought he was dead.

00:17:31.946 --> 00:17:35.252
Clark put his left hand on Lex's body.

00:17:35.312 --> 00:17:38.644
Then he put his right hand over his left.

00:17:38.704 --> 00:17:39.735
One.

00:17:39.795 --> 00:17:40.625
Two.

00:17:40.685 --> 00:17:41.416
One.

00:17:41.476 --> 00:17:42.216
Two.

00:17:42.276 --> 00:17:42.936
One.

00:17:42.996 --> 00:17:43.737
Two.

00:17:43.797 --> 00:17:44.657
Come on.

00:17:44.717 --> 00:17:47.098
Don't die, he said.

00:17:47.158 --> 00:17:50.180
Some water came out of Lex's mouth.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:53.382
He opened his eyes and saw Clark.

00:17:53.442 --> 00:17:55.776
He was very surprised.

00:17:55.836 --> 00:17:59.372
But I hid you, he said.

00:17:59.432 --> 00:18:03.524
Well, I'm not dead, said Clark.

00:18:03.584 --> 00:18:06.346
Clark looked at the bridge.

00:18:06.406 --> 00:18:10.800
A car hit me at a hundred kilometers an hour.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.570
I'm not hurt.

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:16.714
I am not normal, he thought.

00:18:16.774 --> 00:18:20.316
The police and the doctor arrived.

00:18:20.376 --> 00:18:23.475
Then Jonathan Kent arrived too.

00:18:23.535 --> 00:18:26.884
Jonathan put his arms around Clark.

00:18:26.944 --> 00:18:28.655
Are you okay, son?

00:18:28.715 --> 00:18:29.896
He asked.

00:18:29.956 --> 00:18:33.088
I'm fine, Dad, said Clark.

00:18:33.148 --> 00:18:35.240
I'm Jonathan Kent.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:39.092
This is my son, Jonathan told a policeman.

00:18:39.152 --> 00:18:42.224
Who was the stupid driver of the car?

00:18:42.284 --> 00:18:45.217
I was, said Lex Luthor.

00:18:45.277 --> 00:18:48.480
You have a very special son, Mr Kent.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.822
He said, you saved my life, Clark.

00:18:51.882 --> 00:18:53.796
How can I thank you?

00:18:53.856 --> 00:18:57.900
Drive more slowly, said Jonathan.

00:18:57.960 --> 00:19:03.684
After dinner that night, Clark went up to his special room in the barn.

00:19:03.744 --> 00:19:06.086
He looked at the night sky.

00:19:06.146 --> 00:19:10.488
Then he looked over at the farmhouse next to the Kent's farm.

00:19:10.548 --> 00:19:14.791
The front door opened and Lana Lang came out.

00:19:14.852 --> 00:19:16.723
Clark smiled.

00:19:16.783 --> 00:19:19.655
But then Whitney came out.

00:19:19.715 --> 00:19:23.114
Whitney put his arms around Lana.

00:19:23.174 --> 00:19:25.081
Are you alone tonight?"

00:19:25.141 --> 00:19:26.302
he asked.

00:19:26.362 --> 00:19:27.513
Yes.

00:19:27.573 --> 00:19:30.706
Aunt Nell's at Lex Luthor's, said Lana.

00:19:30.766 --> 00:19:32.596
Did you hear about Clark?

00:19:32.656 --> 00:19:33.568
She said.

00:19:33.628 --> 00:19:36.160
He saved Lex's life today.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:37.590
Clark?

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:38.872
Whitney said.

00:19:38.932 --> 00:19:40.502
Clark Kent?

00:19:40.562 --> 00:19:42.984
Yes, said Lana.

00:19:43.044 --> 00:19:46.066
Sometimes people can surprise you.

00:19:46.126 --> 00:19:48.878
Whitney didn't want to talk about Clark.

00:19:48.938 --> 00:19:51.346
He wanted to talk about Whitney.

00:19:51.406 --> 00:19:54.736
I've got a game on Saturday," he said.

00:19:54.796 --> 00:19:57.458
Some important people are going to be there.

00:19:57.518 --> 00:20:00.180
That's great, Lana said.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:03.242
Whitney wanted to be a top football player.

00:20:03.302 --> 00:20:04.934
It was his dream.

00:20:04.994 --> 00:20:07.766
She gave her green necklace to him.

00:20:07.826 --> 00:20:12.430
The necklace was part of a meteor, a special meteor.

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:16.460
This meteor hit Lana's parents' car.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:20.219
I can't take this, Lana," Whitney said.

00:20:20.279 --> 00:20:22.580
It means everything to you.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:25.841
Keep it just for the game, she said.

00:20:25.901 --> 00:20:27.932
He put it in his jacket.

00:20:27.992 --> 00:20:36.154
Then he kissed her.

00:20:36.214 --> 00:20:50.072
Chapter 5 The True Story Tony Carrozza had a job at a car place.

00:20:50.132 --> 00:20:51.452
It was evening.

00:20:51.512 --> 00:20:54.144
It was almost time to go home.

00:20:54.204 --> 00:20:56.564
A boy came into the shop.

00:20:56.625 --> 00:20:58.855
I'm sorry, said Tony.

00:20:58.915 --> 00:21:00.286
We're closed.

00:21:00.346 --> 00:21:02.367
The boy said nothing.

00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:04.928
Tony looked at him carefully.

00:21:04.988 --> 00:21:07.529
I know you, he said.

00:21:07.589 --> 00:21:09.850
You were that scarecrow years ago.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.121
What happened to you?

00:21:12.181 --> 00:21:14.518
Why aren't you older?

00:21:14.578 --> 00:21:17.164
The boy still said nothing.

00:21:17.224 --> 00:21:18.945
Answer me, stupid!"

00:21:19.005 --> 00:21:19.976
said Tony.

00:21:20.036 --> 00:21:21.976
I'm talking to you.

00:21:22.036 --> 00:21:25.347
The boy suddenly hit Tony in the face.

00:21:25.407 --> 00:21:31.139
A big blue electric shock went from his hand into Tony Carotza's body.

00:21:31.199 --> 00:21:33.670
Tony crashed onto the floor.

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:35.630
He didn't move.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:40.772
On the wall, there was a photo of three happy football players.

00:21:40.832 --> 00:21:44.569
The boy smiled and left the shop.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:53.092
It was the day after the car crash, when Clark walked into school, every student said, nice work, Clark.

00:21:53.152 --> 00:21:55.193
Am I at the right school?

00:21:55.254 --> 00:21:57.306
Clark asked Pete and Chloe.

00:21:57.366 --> 00:22:00.968
You saved Lex Luthor's life, said Chloe.

00:22:01.028 --> 00:22:04.230
This is going in the school newspaper.

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:08.414
My dad hates the luthas, said Pete.

00:22:08.474 --> 00:22:15.958
Yes, but Lionel Luthor bought your dad's factory, not Lex, said Clark.

00:22:16.019 --> 00:22:23.352
When Clark arrived home on the farm that afternoon, he found a new red car in front of the house.

00:22:23.412 --> 00:22:25.703
There was a letter on the car.

00:22:25.763 --> 00:22:27.694
Clark opened it.

00:22:27.754 --> 00:22:30.596
Thank you, Clark, he read.

00:22:30.656 --> 00:22:33.117
I hope you like Red.

00:22:33.178 --> 00:22:35.339
Clark looked at the car.

00:22:35.399 --> 00:22:37.480
He was very excited.

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:41.210
You can't keep it, Clark, Jonathan said.

00:22:41.270 --> 00:22:42.808
Why not?

00:22:42.868 --> 00:22:45.799
Because the Luther's aren't good people.

00:22:45.859 --> 00:22:48.220
They're rich thanks to Smallville.

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:51.731
They bought our friends' houses and their farms.

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:55.182
Lex's father did all that, said Clark.

00:22:55.242 --> 00:22:56.932
Not Lex.

00:22:56.992 --> 00:23:00.083
I'm sorry, Clark, Jonathan said.

00:23:00.143 --> 00:23:01.903
I know you're angry.

00:23:01.963 --> 00:23:03.173
Angry?

00:23:03.234 --> 00:23:04.384
Shouted Clark.

00:23:04.444 --> 00:23:06.624
You have no idea.

00:23:06.684 --> 00:23:09.924
He ran up to his room in the barn.

00:23:09.984 --> 00:23:14.216
You must tell him now, Martha said.

00:23:14.276 --> 00:23:17.157
Jonathan went to Clark's room.

00:23:17.217 --> 00:23:20.078
He put his arms around his son.

00:23:20.138 --> 00:23:25.642
I'm going to tell you the story of the day of the meteors, he said.

00:23:25.702 --> 00:23:27.794
He gave Clark a picture.

00:23:27.854 --> 00:23:30.696
There were lots of letters and numbers on it.

00:23:30.756 --> 00:23:32.977
Was it a language?

00:23:33.037 --> 00:23:37.570
I think this is from your mum and dad, he said.

00:23:37.630 --> 00:23:39.532
What does it say?

00:23:39.592 --> 00:23:41.518
Clark asked.

00:23:41.577 --> 00:23:44.654
I have no idea," said Jonathan.

00:23:44.714 --> 00:23:47.446
They came from a different world.

00:23:47.506 --> 00:23:50.588
A different world, laughed Clark.

00:23:50.648 --> 00:23:53.680
So I arrived in a spaceship.

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:55.702
That's stupid.

00:23:55.762 --> 00:23:58.273
Do you want to see that spaceship?

00:23:58.333 --> 00:23:59.654
Asked Jonathan.

00:23:59.714 --> 00:24:01.885
It's under the barn.

00:24:01.946 --> 00:24:06.910
When he saw the little spaceship, Clark was very angry.

00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:09.394
Why didn't you tell me this before?

00:24:09.454 --> 00:24:10.586
He shouted.

00:24:10.646 --> 00:24:19.034
He ran out of the barn.

00:24:19.094 --> 00:24:37.518
Chapter 6 A Quick Kiss Lana Lang looked at the words, Lewis Lang, 1957 to 1989.

00:24:37.578 --> 00:24:42.710
Laura Lang, 1959 to 1989.

00:24:42.770 --> 00:24:45.152
She heard something behind her.

00:24:45.212 --> 00:24:46.393
Who's there?

00:24:46.453 --> 00:24:47.674
She called.

00:24:47.734 --> 00:24:51.236
It's me, it's Clark, he said.

00:24:51.296 --> 00:24:53.632
What are you doing here?

00:24:53.692 --> 00:24:55.987
Lana looked at Clark.

00:24:56.047 --> 00:24:57.538
He was nice.

00:24:57.598 --> 00:25:00.448
Please don't tell anyone, she said.

00:25:00.508 --> 00:25:03.239
I come here to talk to my mum and dad.

00:25:03.299 --> 00:25:04.979
Is that stupid?

00:25:05.039 --> 00:25:08.620
No, it isn't stupid, Clark said.

00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.460
Do you remember them?

00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:13.321
Not very well, said Lana.

00:25:13.381 --> 00:25:15.561
They died when I was three.

00:25:15.621 --> 00:25:17.982
Do you want to meet them?

00:25:18.042 --> 00:25:20.425
She sat on the ground.

00:25:20.485 --> 00:25:25.680
Mum, Dad, this is Clark Kent, she said.

00:25:25.740 --> 00:25:29.582
Hi, Mr. and Mrs. Lang, said Clark.

00:25:29.642 --> 00:25:31.324
I'm sorry?

00:25:31.384 --> 00:25:32.734
What's that?

00:25:32.794 --> 00:25:35.396
He sat down and listened.

00:25:35.456 --> 00:25:40.939
Your mum says, you're never alone, Lana, he said.

00:25:40.999 --> 00:25:44.823
And your dad says, you're beautiful.

00:25:44.883 --> 00:25:47.046
Lana smiled.

00:25:47.106 --> 00:25:49.928
Thank you, Clark, she said.

00:25:49.988 --> 00:25:51.988
Can I walk home with you?

00:25:52.048 --> 00:25:53.550
asked Clark.

00:25:53.610 --> 00:25:56.721
Yes, thanks, said Lana.

00:25:56.781 --> 00:26:03.414
When they arrived at Lana's house, she said, we talked for a long time tonight, Clark.

00:26:03.474 --> 00:26:05.066
It was nice.

00:26:05.126 --> 00:26:07.236
She kissed him quickly.

00:26:07.297 --> 00:26:08.938
Good night, Clark.

00:26:08.998 --> 00:26:11.228
She ran into the house.

00:26:11.288 --> 00:26:13.986
Clark was very happy.

00:26:14.047 --> 00:26:16.954
But there was someone at Lana's house.

00:26:17.014 --> 00:26:21.067
He saw the kiss, and he was very angry.

00:26:21.127 --> 00:26:23.808
It was Whitney Fordman.

00:26:23.868 --> 00:26:29.922
The next day before school, Clark drove the red car back to Lex Luthor's house.

00:26:29.982 --> 00:26:32.404
The house was big and old.

00:26:32.464 --> 00:26:34.344
The front door was open.

00:26:34.404 --> 00:26:36.156
Clark walked in.

00:26:36.216 --> 00:26:37.356
Hello?

00:26:37.416 --> 00:26:38.557
He shouted.

00:26:38.617 --> 00:26:40.682
Is anyone at home?

00:26:40.742 --> 00:26:43.406
Clark, said Lex.

00:26:43.466 --> 00:26:45.078
What are you doing here?

00:26:45.138 --> 00:26:46.900
How's your new car?

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:49.281
I love it, said Clark.

00:26:49.341 --> 00:26:52.494
But I can't keep it.

00:26:52.554 --> 00:26:54.194
Why not?

00:26:54.254 --> 00:26:56.566
You saved my life, Clark.

00:26:56.626 --> 00:26:58.408
I want to thank you.

00:26:58.469 --> 00:26:59.840
Lex said.

00:26:59.900 --> 00:27:03.412
Then he said, oh, I get it.

00:27:03.472 --> 00:27:05.433
Your dad doesn't like me.

00:27:05.494 --> 00:27:07.616
Clark didn't say anything.

00:27:07.676 --> 00:27:09.967
It's okay, said Lex.

00:27:10.027 --> 00:27:11.825
I understand.

00:27:11.885 --> 00:27:14.683
It's not you," said Clark.

00:27:14.744 --> 00:27:17.106
He doesn't like your father.

00:27:17.166 --> 00:27:19.308
Thank you for the car, Lex.

00:27:19.368 --> 00:27:21.799
I'm sorry I can't keep it.

00:27:21.860 --> 00:27:25.384
I changed after that crash, said Lex.

00:27:25.444 --> 00:27:31.470
When I was under the water, I saw my life in Smallville in a new way.

00:27:31.530 --> 00:27:33.280
I can see now.

00:27:33.340 --> 00:27:36.823
This isn't the end of my old life in Metropolis.

00:27:36.883 --> 00:27:39.875
It's the start of my new life here.

00:27:39.936 --> 00:27:41.867
So thank you, Clark.

00:27:41.927 --> 00:27:51.452
I hope we can be friends for a long time.

00:27:51.512 --> 00:28:08.644
Chapter 7 This year's scarecrow When school finished that afternoon, Chloe and Pete went into town.

00:28:08.704 --> 00:28:14.740
There were people and police cars in front of one of the shops, and a man was on the ground.

00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:16.571
What happened here?

00:28:16.631 --> 00:28:18.142
asked Chloe.

00:28:18.202 --> 00:28:20.114
It's Freddy Post.

00:28:20.174 --> 00:28:23.565
He had a big electric shock, said a man.

00:28:23.625 --> 00:28:25.814
Chloe turned to Pete.

00:28:25.875 --> 00:28:29.398
He's the third one this week, she said.

00:28:29.458 --> 00:28:31.950
And here's something interesting.

00:28:32.010 --> 00:28:36.714
They were all in the school football team in 1989.

00:28:36.774 --> 00:28:39.958
Pete looked at the people by the body.

00:28:40.018 --> 00:28:42.430
He saw a teenage boy.

00:28:42.490 --> 00:28:44.162
Who's that boy?

00:28:44.222 --> 00:28:45.432
He asked.

00:28:45.492 --> 00:28:48.056
I don't know, said Chloe.

00:28:48.116 --> 00:28:50.691
She quickly took a photo of him.

00:28:50.751 --> 00:28:55.918
The two friends walked back to the school and went to the newspaper room.

00:28:55.978 --> 00:29:00.590
I'm going to put this photo into the computer, she said.

00:29:00.650 --> 00:29:04.362
Can you find the 1989 year book, Pete?

00:29:04.423 --> 00:29:08.705
A few minutes later, Pete sat next to Chloe with the book.

00:29:08.765 --> 00:29:11.236
Chloe, look, he said.

00:29:11.297 --> 00:29:17.542
This boy, 12 years ago, his name's Jeremy Creek.

00:29:17.602 --> 00:29:21.288
Chloe looked at the book and then at her photo.

00:29:21.348 --> 00:29:24.360
It's the same person, she said.

00:29:24.420 --> 00:29:27.032
And he's the same age.

00:29:27.092 --> 00:29:29.254
That's interesting.

00:29:29.314 --> 00:29:32.866
Chloe and Pete used the internet and wrote emails.

00:29:32.926 --> 00:29:35.238
They found old newspapers.

00:29:35.298 --> 00:29:38.231
I'm going to find Clark, said Pete.

00:29:38.291 --> 00:29:40.762
We must tell him about this.

00:29:40.822 --> 00:29:43.766
Pete came back with Clark.

00:29:43.826 --> 00:29:48.144
Clark looked at the two photos of Jeremy Creek.

00:29:48.204 --> 00:29:53.862
Jeremy had a big electric shock 12 years ago, said Chloe.

00:29:53.922 --> 00:29:56.944
He was in hospital for 12 years.

00:29:57.004 --> 00:30:01.076
A few days ago, he woke up and ran away.

00:30:01.136 --> 00:30:04.298
So, why is he back in Smallville?

00:30:04.358 --> 00:30:05.608
asked Clark.

00:30:05.668 --> 00:30:08.880
Why is he giving electric shocks to people?

00:30:08.941 --> 00:30:14.834
Because 12 years ago, Pete said, they put him on a pole in a field.

00:30:14.894 --> 00:30:17.400
He was that year's scarecrow.

00:30:17.460 --> 00:30:22.478
The Meteors crashed into Smallville that day, said Chloe.

00:30:22.538 --> 00:30:24.050
Oh no!

00:30:24.110 --> 00:30:25.450
thought Clark.

00:30:25.510 --> 00:30:28.102
All this happened because of me.

00:30:28.162 --> 00:30:31.304
That was the day of my arrival.

00:30:31.364 --> 00:30:35.226
He looked at a photo in one of the old newspapers.

00:30:35.286 --> 00:30:36.996
It was a little girl.

00:30:37.057 --> 00:30:39.778
She had a terrible look on her face.

00:30:39.838 --> 00:30:45.292
It said, under the photo, Meteor hits mum and dad.

00:30:45.352 --> 00:30:48.164
So, what do you think, Clark?

00:30:48.224 --> 00:30:49.796
asked Chloe.

00:30:49.856 --> 00:30:53.508
Clark knew that little face in the photo.

00:30:53.568 --> 00:30:55.300
Oh, no.

00:30:55.360 --> 00:30:56.981
Lana.

00:30:57.042 --> 00:30:59.984
Why didn't you tell me about this before?

00:31:00.044 --> 00:31:01.094
He shouted.

00:31:01.154 --> 00:31:02.916
I did this.

00:31:02.976 --> 00:31:05.618
He ran from the room.

00:31:05.678 --> 00:31:09.030
In front of the school, he met Whitney.

00:31:09.090 --> 00:31:11.422
Hi, Clark, said Whitney.

00:31:11.482 --> 00:31:13.024
I'm looking for you.

00:31:13.084 --> 00:31:15.510
You're this year's Scarecrow.

00:31:15.570 --> 00:31:18.786
"'Leave me alone, Whitney,' said Clark angrily.

00:31:18.806 --> 00:31:20.477
"'Or I'm going to.

00:31:20.537 --> 00:31:22.117
You're going to what?'

00:31:22.177 --> 00:31:22.888
said Whitney.

00:31:22.908 --> 00:31:24.548
"'Come on, Clark.

00:31:24.608 --> 00:31:25.618
Hit me.'

00:31:25.678 --> 00:31:27.509
He took off his jacket.

00:31:27.569 --> 00:31:32.651
Clark moved nearer to Whitney, but he suddenly started to fall.

00:31:32.711 --> 00:31:36.713
He saw Lana's green necklace under Whitney's open t-shirt.

00:31:36.733 --> 00:31:39.474
"'What's between you and Lana?'

00:31:39.534 --> 00:31:40.354
shouted Whitney.

00:31:40.374 --> 00:31:43.052
"'You can have her necklace.'

00:31:43.112 --> 00:31:48.494
He took off the necklace and put it on Clark, but you can't have Lana.

00:31:48.554 --> 00:31:51.126
I'm taking her to the dance tonight.

00:31:51.186 --> 00:31:53.398
Clark didn't feel well.

00:31:53.458 --> 00:31:57.432
He tried to move and then everything went black.

00:31:57.492 --> 00:32:01.226
Whitney and two of his friends put him in a car.

00:32:01.286 --> 00:32:14.203
Jeremy Creek watched everything and he remembered this day 12 years ago.

00:32:14.264 --> 00:32:22.316
Chapter 8.

00:32:22.376 --> 00:32:25.266
A big red S.

00:32:25.326 --> 00:32:27.687
Clark woke up.

00:32:27.747 --> 00:32:30.578
He was in a cornfield on a pole.

00:32:30.638 --> 00:32:32.478
He was very cold.

00:32:32.538 --> 00:32:35.329
It was night, and it was October.

00:32:35.389 --> 00:32:37.000
He looked down.

00:32:37.060 --> 00:32:40.630
There was a big red S on the front of his body.

00:32:40.690 --> 00:32:43.081
He tried to move his arms.

00:32:43.141 --> 00:32:44.792
I can't move.

00:32:44.852 --> 00:32:46.242
What's wrong with me?

00:32:46.302 --> 00:32:47.442
He thought.

00:32:47.502 --> 00:32:49.808
It's the necklace.

00:32:49.868 --> 00:32:53.706
Suddenly, there was a boy in front of him.

00:32:53.766 --> 00:32:56.588
It hurts, said the boy.

00:32:56.648 --> 00:32:58.539
I remember that.

00:32:58.600 --> 00:33:01.842
Your Jeremy Creek, said Clark.

00:33:01.902 --> 00:33:03.174
No.

00:33:03.234 --> 00:33:07.387
Jeremy Creek died 12 years ago, said the boy.

00:33:07.448 --> 00:33:09.799
He started to walk away.

00:33:09.860 --> 00:33:11.671
Where are you going?

00:33:11.731 --> 00:33:12.942
asked Clark.

00:33:13.002 --> 00:33:16.034
To the school dance, said Jeremy.

00:33:16.095 --> 00:33:18.382
I didn't go in 1989.

00:33:18.442 --> 00:33:21.911
Please help me," said Clark.

00:33:21.971 --> 00:33:24.414
No, Jeremy said.

00:33:24.474 --> 00:33:26.276
You stay here.

00:33:26.336 --> 00:33:28.899
I don't want to hurt you.

00:33:28.959 --> 00:33:31.692
Jeremy walked down the road.

00:33:31.752 --> 00:33:34.776
Lex Luthor drove by and saw him.

00:33:34.836 --> 00:33:37.570
I know that boy, he thought.

00:33:37.630 --> 00:33:38.830
But how?

00:33:38.890 --> 00:33:40.417
From where?

00:33:40.477 --> 00:33:42.374
He stopped the car.

00:33:42.434 --> 00:33:45.346
Then he remembered the field twelve years ago.

00:33:45.406 --> 00:33:48.779
The boy on the pole, the big red s.

00:33:48.840 --> 00:33:52.554
He got out of the car and went into the field.

00:33:52.614 --> 00:33:55.026
Help me, he heard.

00:33:55.086 --> 00:33:57.168
Help me please.

00:33:57.228 --> 00:33:58.940
It's not possible.

00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:00.271
Lex thought.

00:34:00.332 --> 00:34:01.833
Then he saw him.

00:34:01.893 --> 00:34:04.200
Clark, he shouted.

00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:06.276
Lex helped Clark.

00:34:06.336 --> 00:34:08.678
Clark pulled off the necklace.

00:34:08.738 --> 00:34:11.950
You need a doctor, Clark, Lex said.

00:34:12.011 --> 00:34:16.434
Without the necklace, Clark was suddenly Clark again.

00:34:16.495 --> 00:34:18.676
He didn't need a doctor.

00:34:18.736 --> 00:34:22.659
I'm okay, thanks Lex, he said.

00:34:22.720 --> 00:34:26.032
He found his clothes and ran into the night.

00:34:26.092 --> 00:34:28.994
Lex saw the necklace on the ground.

00:34:29.055 --> 00:34:33.521
He put it in his jacket and walked back to his car.

00:34:33.581 --> 00:34:38.496
At the school dance, the band played and everyone danced.

00:34:38.557 --> 00:34:41.088
Jeremy Creek didn't dance.

00:34:41.148 --> 00:34:43.658
He was behind the school building.

00:34:43.718 --> 00:34:46.760
He opened the door of a large box.

00:34:46.820 --> 00:34:49.120
Water, it said.

00:34:49.181 --> 00:34:52.592
They're all going to die now, he thought.

00:34:52.652 --> 00:34:55.193
Suddenly Clark was behind him.

00:34:55.253 --> 00:34:58.284
Stop this now, Jeremy, he said.

00:34:58.344 --> 00:35:00.705
You, said Jeremy.

00:35:00.765 --> 00:35:02.622
What are you doing here?

00:35:02.682 --> 00:35:06.230
You're not going to hurt my friends, said Clark."

00:35:06.290 --> 00:35:09.261
You don't understand, said Jeremy.

00:35:09.321 --> 00:35:12.192
I'm doing this for you and the others.

00:35:12.252 --> 00:35:14.453
No more scarecrows.

00:35:14.513 --> 00:35:15.714
No, Jeremy.

00:35:15.774 --> 00:35:17.894
Stop it, said Clark.

00:35:17.954 --> 00:35:22.106
Jeremy hit Clark in the face, but he had a surprise.

00:35:22.166 --> 00:35:24.490
Clark wasn't hurt.

00:35:24.550 --> 00:35:27.283
There was a car next to Jeremy.

00:35:27.343 --> 00:35:29.474
He opened the door and started it.

00:35:29.534 --> 00:35:31.324
He drove at Clark.

00:35:31.384 --> 00:35:35.866
Clark put his arms in front of him, but Jeremy didn't stop.

00:35:35.926 --> 00:35:39.758
Clark was on the front of the car when it hit the water box.

00:35:39.818 --> 00:35:42.038
There was water everywhere.

00:35:42.098 --> 00:35:45.100
It gave Jeremy a big electric shock.

00:35:45.160 --> 00:35:46.980
His body was blue.

00:35:47.040 --> 00:35:49.612
Then everything was quiet.

00:35:49.672 --> 00:35:52.012
Clark pulled the car door.

00:35:52.072 --> 00:35:53.380
It opened.

00:35:53.440 --> 00:35:54.928
Are you okay?"

00:35:54.988 --> 00:35:56.148
he asked.

00:35:56.208 --> 00:35:57.679
Who are you?

00:35:57.739 --> 00:35:59.110
asked Jeremy.

00:35:59.170 --> 00:36:01.440
I want to go home.

00:36:01.500 --> 00:36:04.952
Clark watched the end of the homecoming dance.

00:36:05.012 --> 00:36:08.393
Lana and Whitney danced in the center of the room.

00:36:08.454 --> 00:36:10.244
Then they kissed.

00:36:10.304 --> 00:36:12.016
A long kiss.

00:36:12.076 --> 00:36:14.006
Clark was sad.

00:36:14.066 --> 00:36:16.458
He turned and left.

00:36:16.518 --> 00:36:20.327
There were three cars in a line in the car park.

00:36:20.387 --> 00:36:24.968
That's Whitney's car and his friend's cars, Clark thought.

00:36:25.028 --> 00:36:27.000
He had an idea.

00:36:27.060 --> 00:36:31.094
He took one car and put it on top of another one.

00:36:31.154 --> 00:36:35.468
Then he took the third car and put it on top of the other two.

00:36:35.529 --> 00:36:37.159
He waited.

00:36:37.220 --> 00:36:41.774
When students came out and saw the cars, they laughed.

00:36:41.834 --> 00:36:45.828
Then Whitney came out with his arm around Lana.

00:36:45.888 --> 00:36:47.582
He saw his car.

00:36:47.642 --> 00:36:49.926
Who did this to my car?

00:36:49.986 --> 00:36:51.647
He shouted angrily.

00:36:51.707 --> 00:37:01.463
Everyone laughed and Lana smiled.

00:37:01.523 --> 00:37:12.018
Epilogue, thanks for the dance.

00:37:12.078 --> 00:37:16.084
Clark called Jonathan when he came home.

00:37:16.145 --> 00:37:17.628
Lex was here.

00:37:17.688 --> 00:37:19.409
This is for you.

00:37:19.469 --> 00:37:23.159
He gave Clark a small box and a letter.

00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:26.020
Lana's necklace was in the box.

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:28.361
Clark read the letter.

00:37:28.421 --> 00:37:31.872
I found this necklace in the cornfield, Clark.

00:37:31.932 --> 00:37:33.462
We're friends now.

00:37:33.522 --> 00:37:35.853
So please keep this box.

00:37:35.913 --> 00:37:38.894
My mother gave it to me many years ago.

00:37:38.954 --> 00:37:40.804
It's very special.

00:37:40.864 --> 00:37:42.454
Lex.

00:37:42.514 --> 00:37:46.916
Clark opened the box and saw the necklace.

00:37:46.976 --> 00:37:50.107
He didn't feel well.

00:37:50.168 --> 00:37:54.199
He closed the box again, and he was okay.

00:37:54.259 --> 00:37:56.660
It was a special box.

00:37:56.720 --> 00:38:00.341
I must remember that, he thought.

00:38:00.401 --> 00:38:02.282
Hello, Clark!

00:38:02.342 --> 00:38:05.093
It was Lana in his room in the barn.

00:38:05.153 --> 00:38:07.703
Lana, he said, surprised.

00:38:07.764 --> 00:38:09.644
What are you doing here?

00:38:09.704 --> 00:38:12.996
You didn't come to the dance, she said.

00:38:13.056 --> 00:38:16.296
She walked up to him and put her arms around him.

00:38:16.357 --> 00:38:18.674
Let's dance now.

00:38:18.734 --> 00:38:21.182
They danced to the music.

00:38:21.242 --> 00:38:23.534
Clark closed his eyes.

00:38:23.594 --> 00:38:25.786
Suddenly he heard a car.

00:38:25.846 --> 00:38:27.518
He opened his eyes.

00:38:27.578 --> 00:38:29.670
Lana wasn't there.

00:38:29.730 --> 00:38:32.055
It was a daydream.

00:38:32.115 --> 00:38:34.019
He looked through the window.

00:38:34.039 --> 00:38:37.091
A car arrived at Lana's house.

00:38:37.151 --> 00:38:38.992
The necklace.

00:38:39.053 --> 00:38:41.564
Clark took it to Lana's house.

00:38:41.624 --> 00:38:43.786
He put it on her front door.

00:38:43.846 --> 00:38:47.518
He was back in his room before Lana opened the car door.

00:38:47.578 --> 00:38:51.666
He moved faster than the wind, and nobody saw him.

00:38:51.726 --> 00:38:56.374
When Lana arrived at her front door, she saw the necklace.

00:38:56.434 --> 00:38:58.816
She took it and put it on.

00:38:58.877 --> 00:39:03.650
Oh, Whitney, you are fantastic, she thought.

00:39:03.710 --> 00:39:05.502
Good night, Lana.

00:39:05.562 --> 00:39:07.554
Clark said quietly.

00:39:07.614 --> 00:39:09.176
Thanks for the dance.

